cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model or its results in your research or policy analysis, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DGE-METRIC: Dynamic General Equilibrium for Macroeconomic Energy Transition Incorporating Carbon Markets"
abstract: >
  DGE-METRIC is a MATLAB/Dynare implementation of a dynamic general equilibrium model
  for studying the macroeconomic consequences of energy-transition pathways, green finance
  instruments, and carbon-pricing policies. The current working calibration covers Vietnam
  (5-sector, 1-region, 2026–2050 horizon) and is applied to Power Development Plan 8 (PDP8)
  and net-zero scenarios under a GIZ-IWH research project.
